# Images are built from ./backend and ./frontend (each has its own .dockerignore). This file protects any build that
# uses the repository root as its context: secrets, databases, patient files and backups never enter an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite*
**/data/
**/uploads/
**/backups/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
.git/
*.pem
*.key
